<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.ConstraintsModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:constraint="org.blockml.bml.constraint"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:diag="org.blockml.bml.diagnostic"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.task"
  xmlns:validation="org.blockml.bml.validation">

  <name>ConstraintsModel</name>
  <type>doc:ConstraintsModel</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to constraints and suggestions</is>

  <documentation>
    Constraints are reusable validation rules attached via a single &lt;constraints&gt; container on
    ConstrainableDefinition elements (Blocks and members). There is no target= property — the
    embedding context binds the constraint automatically. Constraint branches declare genericTypes;
    the compiler binds T from context (never authored):
    • ValueConstraint on Property → T = effective ValueType
    • PropertyConstraint → T = PropertyDefinition
    • AggregationConstraint / AssociationConstraint / CapabilityConstraint → corresponding Definition
    • BlockConstraint → BlockDefinition (incl. Sub-/Root-)
    Wrong branch for context → BML_CONSTRAINT_TARGET_MISMATCH. Unknown constraint type →
    BML_CONSTRAINT_UNKNOWN. Generic T incompatible → BML_CONSTRAINT_TYPE_MISMATCH. Instance property
    incompatible with T → BML_CONSTRAINT_VALUE_MISMATCH.

    Validation property (optional) references org.blockml.bml.validation.*:
    • Error → BML_CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION (fail compile)
    • Warning → BML_CONSTRAINT_WARNING
    • Information → BML_CONSTRAINT_INFORMATION
    Omitted validation → constraint is metadata only (not value-enforced by the BlockML validator).

    Standard value constraints include Min, Max, MinLength, MaxLength, MinItems, MaxItems, Pattern,
    ValuePresent. Structural examples: RequiresMember, AllowedChildType, NoSelfReference,
    MustBeReadOnly, RequiresImplementation. Prefer ValueType instance configuration for
    type-intrinsic thresholds (Text{maxLength: 100}); keep Constraints for contextual/composable
    rules (doc:ValueTypeConfiguration).

    Suggestions — Property-only metadata: Block instances compatible with the property type for
    editors/renderers. Not validation. Forbidden on EnumType properties → BML_SUGGESTIONS_ON_ENUM.
    Incompatible suggestion instance → BML_SUGGESTION_TYPE_MISMATCH (PrimitiveType properties use
    matching *Entity wrappers).

    Procedure: task:AddConstraint.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="def:ConstrainableDefinition" relation="Defines">
      Shared constraints container on Blocks and members.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Constraint" relation="Extends">
      Constraint branch root.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Validation" relation="Defines">
      Error / Warning / Information enforcement markers.
    </see>
    <see type="constraint:Min" relation="SeeAlso">
      Example scalar constraint.
    </see>
    <see type="constraint:Pattern" relation="SeeAlso">
      Example textual constraint.
    </see>
    <see type="def:PropertyDefinition" relation="SeeAlso">
      suggestions aggregation and property constraints.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:ValueTypeConfiguration" relation="SeeAlso">
      Prefer inline configuration for type-intrinsic thresholds.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:GenericsModel" relation="SeeAlso">
      Constraint generic binding from embedding context.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:ModelingGuidelines" relation="SeeAlso">
      When to use constraints in modeling.
    </see>
    <see type="task:AddConstraint" relation="SeeAlso">
      Procedural how-to for attaching constraints.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_CONSTRAINT_TARGET_MISMATCH" relation="SeeAlso">
      Branch ↔ context incompatibility.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_SUGGESTIONS_ON_ENUM" relation="SeeAlso">
      Suggestions forbidden on EnumType properties.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:MemberVisibility" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — member and Sub-Block visibility (README learning order).
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
